   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# CIA II – Business Data Analysis and Visualization Using Python\n",
    "\n",
    "## Retail Sales and Profitability Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Course:** Business Data Analysis / Python  \n",
    "**Programme:** BBA (Strategy and Business Analytics)  \n",
    "**Institution:** CHRIST (Deemed to be University), School of Business and Management, Bannerghatta Road Campus  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Group Members\n",
    "1. **Rupesh**\n", (2523250)
    "2. **Sarvesh**\n", (2523273)
    "3. **Anik**\n", (2523225)
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This project performs an end-to-end business data analysis on a retail sales dataset using **NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn**. The analysis covers:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset inspection and quality assessment\n",
    "- Missing-value and duplicate handling\n",
    "- Data-type conversion and feature engineering\n",
    "- Statistical analysis and aggregation\n",
    "- Sales, profit, discount, category, region, and customer-segment analysis\n",
    "- Professional business visualizations\n",
    "- Executive dashboard/reporting\n",
    "- Business insights and recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Academic dataset note:** The dataset used for this project is a synthetic retail dataset created for academic demonstration. It is not presented as proprietary company data.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1517fb23",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Business Problem and Objectives"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2340356e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Business Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "A retail business needs to understand **where revenue is being generated, where profit is being lost, and whether discounting is supporting or damaging profitability**. Management also needs to identify the strongest categories, regions, segments, and time periods.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Clean and transform the retail dataset accurately.\n",
    "2. Use Pandas and NumPy to calculate business performance metrics.\n",
    "3. Identify sales and profit trends across time, products, regions, and customer segments.\n",
    "4. Examine the relationship between discounting and profitability.\n",
    "5. Communicate the findings through professional visualizations and an executive dashboard.\n",
    "6. Convert analytical findings into actionable business recommendations.\n"
   ]
  },
