    "\n",
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Category strategy:** Focus resources on the category generating the strongest profit while reviewing the economics of weaker categories.\n",
    "- **Regional strategy:** The strongest region can be used as a benchmark for pricing, product mix, and sales practices.\n",
    "- **Segment strategy:** The largest customer segment provides a useful base for targeted retention and cross-selling initiatives.\n",
    "- **Discount strategy:** Higher discounting should not be evaluated using sales alone; management should monitor the effect on profit and margin.\n",
    "- **Profitability monitoring:** Loss-making sub-categories require SKU-level or promotion-level investigation before additional discounting or expansion.\n",
    "- **Seasonality:** Monthly changes in sales and profit can help management plan inventory, promotions, staffing, and working capital.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e74c70b1",
